[COMMENTS]
STATION,Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume. Long term IH/UKCEH research catchment. Natural flow regime. GENERAL: Rectangular, side contracted critical depth flume designed by Hydraulics Research Ltd, suitable for streams with steep gradients, heavy sediment loads and high flood/drought flow ratios. Catchment nested within Cefn Brwyn (55008). Primary 15 minute dataset available. STATION HYDROMETRY: Shoal formation common, requiring prompt removal to avoid drowning. Check gauged by c/m, and volumetrically at lowest flows. FLOW RECORD: Daily mean flows replaced from 01/10/1973 to 31/12/2010, and AMAX flows from 01/10/1973 to 01/10/2010 following detailed QC (August 2025, WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Responsive flow regime. Natural to within 10% at Q95.
CATCHMENT,Very wet catchment; drains Plynlimon massif. Composed of Ordovician grits, shales and slates and Silurian mudstones, mostly covered by peaty soils. Mainly natural or partly reseeded grassland, supporting sheep grazing.
Qmed Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
Pooling Suitability,No rating or gaugings available.
